# Ambiguity: a formal place x and a Structure x in the data group of the header are two occurrences of the name x, so the bare x of the code is ambiguous --
# not a statement on the place (#data-code-roles, #structure-index: a name that more than one occurrence of the data holds needs its index). The answer is 3.
(
    Observed:
        int: result 0
)
@: shared data[0]
fn: wrong (int: x) int (x(int: y 1))
    return: x
int: result wrong(7)

sub: main ()
    shared\Observed\result := result
main()
